# Sequential Workflows in LangGraph | Agentic AI using LangGraph | Video 5 | CampusX

A sequential workflow is a pipeline where tasks execute in a strictly linear order without branching or parallel paths. The session has two central goals: teaching the foundational coding patterns and syntax of LangGraph, and enabling learners to independently construct any linear workflow. Through three progressive implementations—a non-LLM BMI Calculator, a single-node LLM Question-Answering pipeline, and a two-stage Prompt Chaining Blog Generator—the tutorial illustrates environment configuration, state schema design using TypedDict, node functions, edge orchestration, compilation, execution, graph visualization, and LangGraph's superior state retention over traditional LangChain chains.

